0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127899" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}k-1 & k-1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(k-1)\\cdot (-1)-(k-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-k+1-3k+3 \\\\  & =-4k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k+4 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127899/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127899"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127906/selection/44855ba0613121a1ddbb17cff307d99cb533fdec60ddec9161b81ae8332a6ab0" :answer/id #uuid "6c2fdb88-f3bd-58dc-8b12-f81fd77e7682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127906/selection/8b5a8474a9b9934bc051275be5cb046d57f79f1810a453d2a6924c7b768a1f5e" :answer/id #uuid "7d18b266-5628-524a-9a64-e368223f98b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127906/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer/id #uuid "b43c0b66-c9ab-5504-b608-bf20041e7163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127906/selection/676f334db9ed10b43d86b3a7db987f2cb2fa3661fe95cf6e833536dc531906d3" :answer/id #uuid "a581bb9e-7427-50b4-96af-004a7ff31eab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127906/selection/a65366fb2e333fe86ff259e927ae0a38521c97202f66a3c47e1eae1bc4f7deb1" :answer/id #uuid "ab9992b3-48f7-53e4-8050-7a875c2e2d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127906/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e7fac3f-7978-5eae-83e0-2e9fefcc1c72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127906/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer-field/choices ["q-127906/selection/44855ba0613121a1ddbb17cff307d99cb533fdec60ddec9161b81ae8332a6ab0" "q-127906/selection/8b5a8474a9b9934bc051275be5cb046d57f79f1810a453d2a6924c7b768a1f5e" "q-127906/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" "q-127906/selection/676f334db9ed10b43d86b3a7db987f2cb2fa3661fe95cf6e833536dc531906d3" "q-127906/selection/a65366fb2e333fe86ff259e927ae0a38521c97202f66a3c47e1eae1bc4f7deb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127906" :question/id #uuid "946cfcad-5219-5323-b969-2d09055140bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-127906" :question/problem "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ t & -8\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot (-8)-t\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8t-2t \\\\  & =-10t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127906/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127906"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-313957/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "26246cc3-18d3-5d50-afc8-70956d030040" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313957/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e63e0873-13fe-5e06-958b-e0422accea72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-313957/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-313957/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-313957/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a51dd8d7-65c0-5bcb-bdd5-3a9418a9ed03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313957/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "48de27c9-df19-5c9b-bf11-5c1264f961db" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-313957/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-313957/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-313957" :question/id #uuid "c2b70825-9a5f-55c4-a501-35637f350b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-313957" :question/problem "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}x-4 & 1 \\\\ 7 & x+2\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-4)\\cdot (x+2)-7\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-8-7 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-15 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-313957/field-1" "q-313957/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-313957"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
